      "message": "Instead of doing a try/catch I would suggest a simple if statement that checks sets `name` if it is anywhere is `args` and then passing the name to the exception if so as such:\n\n    # We traverse in case name is in args[0] .... args[n]\n    name \u003d \u0027 \u0027\n    for item in args:\n         if hasattr(args, \u0027name\u0027):\n              name \u003d getattr(item, \u0027name\u0027)\n\n     raise exception.Conflict(type\u003dconflict_type, name\u003dname,\n                                             details\u003d_(\u0027Duplicate Entry\u0027))\n\nI Rodrigo suggested, using python\u0027s hasattr() is a more readable and maintainable. This may also address Dave\u0027s comment of the value possibly being in different positions.",
